@meta
id: 14-16
title: Drill — swap the arguments
chapter: 14
type: drill
skills: sub-backref
par: 56
minutes: 5
reps: 8
vscode: a regex replace with $2, $1, typed carefully
open: refund.calls.ts

@brief
Eight times: `refund` used to take `(amount, orderId)` and now takes
`(orderId, amount)`. Five call sites, two groups, one substitute.

You are drilling the shape of a swap until the groups and the
references come out in the right order without thinking.

@keys
| `\v(\w+), (\w+)` | two groups: a word, a comma, a word |
| `\2, \1` | the same two, the other way round |

@hints
Capture the two arguments as two groups. Write `refund(` and `)`
around them in both halves so nothing else with a comma matches.
--
`:%s/\vrefund\((\w+), (\w+)\)/refund(\2, \1)/` and Enter.

@solution
    :%s/\vrefund\((\w+), (\w+)\)/refund(\2, \1)/<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Forty-nine keystrokes. The `refund\(` at the front is what keeps the
other comma-separated pairs in the file out of it; the `\w+` groups are
what makes the five different argument names irrelevant. If the swap
feels slower than editing five lines by hand, count the keystrokes for
one line by hand and multiply by five.

@start refund.calls.ts
export async function settle(orderId: string, amount: number, fee: number, deposit: number) {
  await paymentService.refund(amount, orderId);
  await paymentService.refund(fee, orderId);
  await ledger.record(orderId, amount);

  if (deposit > 0) {
    await paymentService.refund(deposit, orderId);
  }

  const partial = Math.round(amount / 2);
  await paymentService.refund(partial, orderId);
  await paymentService.refund(fee, orderId);
}

@expected refund.calls.ts
export async function settle(orderId: string, amount: number, fee: number, deposit: number) {
  await paymentService.refund(orderId, amount);
  await paymentService.refund(orderId, fee);
  await ledger.record(orderId, amount);

  if (deposit > 0) {
    await paymentService.refund(orderId, deposit);
  }

  const partial = Math.round(amount / 2);
  await paymentService.refund(orderId, partial);
  await paymentService.refund(orderId, fee);
}
